<title>UK: Austria trade bids for free mkt grain at EU tender.</title>
<headline>Austria trade bids for free mkt grain at EU tender.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian traders have submitted bids for 9,000 tonnes of free market wheat and 1,050 tonnes of free market barley at Thursday's EU grains tender, member state officials said.</p>
<p>The bids on wheat are for a refund ranging from 0.00 to 0.50 Ecus per tonne, the officials said. On barley a refund of 27.10 Ecus is sought.</p>
<p>The EU cereals management committee will adjudicate tender bids at its meeting on Thursday afternoon.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
